        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(cron): explicit cron wakes bypass heartbeat quiet-hours gate (#105413)",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes #105413.\n\nMain-session cron jobs (`sessionTarget: \"main\"` + `payload.kind: \"systemEvent\"`) are executed by delegating to the heartbeat runner: `executeMainSessionCronJob` enqueues the payload as a `SystemEvent` with `contextKey: \"cron:<jobId>\"` and then calls `runHeartbeatOnce({ source: \"cron\", intent: \"immediate\", reason: \"cron:<jobId>\", heartbeat: { target: \"last\" } })` (see `src/cron/service/timer.ts`).\n\nThe heartbeat active-hours (“quiet-hours”) gate in `runHeartbeatOnce` was checked **before** the queued cron event was ever inspected:\n\n```ts\n// src/infra/heartbeat-runner.ts (pre-fix)\nif (!isWithinActiveHours(cfg, heartbeat, startedAt)) {\n  return { status: \"skipped\", reason: \"quiet-hours\" };\n}\n```\n\nSo any main/systemEvent cron scheduled outside `heartbeat.activeHours` was silently skipped with `last_error: \"quiet-hours\"`, and its `payload.text` never reached a model turn. Reporter confirmed this deterministically on every fire since upgrading `2026.4.27 → 2026.6.11` (e.g. a `55 3 * * *` nightly flush job).\n\n`activeHours` is meant to bound *scheduled heartbeat polls*, not cron job execution. This PR draws that line.\n\n## Evidence\n\nFix (`src/infra/heartbeat-runner.ts`, around line 1459): let explicit cron wakes bypass the active-hours gate. Ordinary scheduled heartbeats keep it — the `activeHours` feature added in `31943dcecb8d` still bounds regular polls.\n\n```ts\nconst wakeSource = opts.source ?? inferHeartbeatWakeSourceFromReason(opts.reason);\nconst isExplicitCronWake = wakeSource === \"cron\";\nif (!isExplicitCronWake && !isWithinActiveHours(cfg, heartbeat, startedAt)) {\n  return { status: \"skipped\", reason: \"quiet-hours\" };\n}\n```\n\nOnce the gate is bypassed, `resolveHeartbeatPreflight` already sets `isCronWake: true` for `source === \"cron\"`, and `resolveHeartbeatRunPrompt` (line 1255) already picks tagged cron events (`preflight.isCronWake || contextKey?.startsWith(\"cron:\")`) and routes them through `buildCronEventPrompt(...)`. So the tagged cron prompt path from commits `54513f424066` / `4c4d2558e34c` (vignesh07) and the delegation contract from `d4e59a3666d8` (mbelinky) are preserved verbatim — nothing else changes.\n\n### Feature interaction summary\n\n| Feature | Introduced in | Behavior after this PR |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `heartbeat.activeHours` quiet-hours skip | `31943dcecb8d` | Preserved for scheduled heartbeats (no `source`) and non-cron wake sources (`exec-event`, `hook`, `acp-spawn`, `session-state`). |\n| Tagged cron event prompt (`buildCronEventPrompt`) | `54513f424066`, `4c4d2558e34c` | Preserved; unchanged. |\n| Cron → heartbeat delegation with `contextKey: \"cron:<jobId>\"` and `target: \"last\"` | `d4e59a3666d8` | Preserved; the delegating call site in `src/cron/service/timer.ts` is unchanged. |\n\n### Tests\n\nAdded `src/infra/heartbeat-runner.cron-bypasses-active-hours.test.ts`:\n\n1. Ordinary scheduled heartbeat (no `source`) outside `activeHours` → `status: \"skipped\", reason: \"quiet-hours\"` (regression guard for `activeHours`).\n2. Explicit `source: \"cron\"` wake outside `activeHours` → `reason !== \"quiet-hours\"` (the #105413 regression).\n3. Cron wake with only `reason: \"cron:...\"` (inferred source path via `inferHeartbeatWakeSourceFromReason`) → `reason !== \"quiet-hours\"`.\n\nExisting coverage exercised by this change without modification:\n\n- `src/infra/heartbeat-runner.returns-default-unset.test.ts` — the “skips outside active hours” case (no `source`) still expects `quiet-hours`; this PR does not alter that path.\n- `src/infra/heartbeat-runner.active-hours-schedule.e2e.test.ts` — scheduler-level quiet-hours advancement is unaffected (scheduler still passes `source: \"cron\"` only for cron entries).\n- `src/cron/service.main-job-passes-heartbeat-target-last.test.ts` — delegation contract and `heartbeat.target = \"last\"` unchanged.\n\nLocal `pnpm` is not installed on this machine (see repo TOOLS notes); no format/lint pass was run beyond `git diff` self-review. Diff is scoped to the two files above.\n\n## Related\n\n- #105257 — same signature (`trigger: \"heartbeat\"` on a cron session with `[OpenClaw heartbeat poll]`) reported for one-shot `at` jobs; a proper cron wake bypass here should also help those.\n- #96663, #84923 — earlier reports of the same class of symptom.\n",
